        "v": 5,
        "title": "Replace MinHeap with sorted array in token pruning",
        "summary": "Refactor `pruneFileTokenScores` in `backend/src/truncate-file-tree.ts` to replace `MinHeap` with a sorted array and heuristic batching. This change optimizes performance by reducing expensive `printFileTreeWithTokens` loop iterations via estimated token removals. The function now returns an object containing `pruned`, `printedTree`, and `tokenCount` instead of just the pruned scores.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T17:08:30.100Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The assistant can now trim down large amounts of file data faster when you ask it to analyze your project. Previously, it used a slow step-by-step process to remove token data; now it estimates how much to cut in fewer passes, which developers noticed as a performance improvement in their tooling. If you trigger project analysis that hits the internal token-pruning logic, the backend completes the task with less waiting, but you won't see a visible UI change. This is live today for anyone using the assistant's project-truncation features.",
